stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> reset
    reset --> initialize: reset complete / auto progression armed
    initialize --> connect: INITIALIZE sent successfully
    initialize --> wait_for_com_reset: COM unavailable / invalid mirrored config / bridge setup failure
    connect --> keepalive: client_connected / mirrored KEEPALIVE / mirrored DATA
    connect --> wait_for_com_reset: bridge reports blocking transport fault
    keepalive --> connect: bridge reports transport loss
    keepalive --> wait_for_com_reset: 5 sequential bridge-reported keepalive failures
    wait_for_com_reset --> reset: explicit Reset Communication

    state reset {
        [*] --> clear_host_state
        clear_host_state --> send_reset
        send_reset --> arm_initialize
    }

    state initialize {
        [*] --> validate_mirrored_config
        validate_mirrored_config --> send_initialize
    }

    state connect {
        [*] --> send_connect
        send_connect --> wait_for_bridge_events
    }

    note right of keepalive
        The ESP32-C3 bridge owns the real
        TCP keepalive watchdog and counter
        supervision. The Python runtime
        mirrors bridge events only.
    end note
